        calling raylib.ImageBlurGaussian with self, blur_size

    ## Applies a convolution kernel to the image.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `kernel`: the convolution kernel; its length must be a perfect square
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## Nothing; the image is changed in place.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## The kernel is typically a 3x3 or 5x5 matrix laid out row by row; the wrapper passes it as a flat slice.
    ## An empty slice is passed straight through, which raylib does not guard against, so the docstring warns.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## Nothing is leaked: every raylib buffer this wrapper allocates or receives is released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling img.convolve with (kernel at 0 to 9)
    ## ```

    weave convolve with kernel as slice of f32 into void:
        if (kernel.length) == 0:
            return
        let raw as ref to void is transmute (sigil of (kernel at 0)) to (ref to void)
        calling raylib.ImageKernelConvolution with self, (transmute raw to ref to frozen f32), (kernel.length)

