    ## Returns every pixel as an owned list of colours.
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## `some` with an owned list of every pixel, or `maybe none` for an invalid image.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## raylib allocates the array for you in one contiguous block; the wrapper copies it into an owned list and releases the raylib buffer, so the result is entirely PenguScript-owned.
    ## `maybe none` when the image is invalid (raylib returned a null pointer).
    ## The list is in row-major order and its length is `width * height`.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## Nothing is leaked: every raylib buffer this wrapper allocates or receives is released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## var pixels as maybe (list of raylib.Color) is calling img.colors
    ## ```

    weave colors into maybe (list of raylib.Color):
        var count as int is ((essence of self).width * (essence of self).height)
        var raw as ref to raylib.Color is calling raylib.LoadImageColors with (essence of self)
        if calling ffi.is_null with (transmute raw to ref to void):
            return maybe none
        let as_void as ref to void is transmute raw to ref to void
        var owned as list of raylib.Color is calling ffi.list_from_ptr of raylib.Color with as_void, count
        calling raylib.UnloadImageColors with raw
        return some owned

    ## Builds the image's colour palette.
    ##
    ## ## Parameters
    ## - `max_size`: the largest palette to build
    ##
    ## ## Returns
    ## An owned `list of raylib.Color`.
    ##
    ## ## Notes
    ## raylib allocates the array and reports its length through an out-parameter; the wrapper copies it and releases the raylib buffer, so the count folds into `.length`.
    ## A solid-colour image yields a one-entry palette, which is a useful thing to assert.
    ##
    ## ## Memory
    ## Nothing is leaked: every raylib buffer this wrapper allocates or receives is released before returning.
    ##
    ## ## Example
    ## ```pengu
    ## var pal as list of raylib.Color is calling img.palette with 16
    ## ```

    weave palette with max_size as int into list of raylib.Color:
        var count as int is 0
        var raw as ref to raylib.Color is calling raylib.LoadImagePalette with (essence of self), max_size, sigil of count
        if calling ffi.is_null with (transmute raw to ref to void):
            return list of raylib.Color
        let as_void as ref to void is transmute raw to ref to void
        var owned as list of raylib.Color is calling ffi.list_from_ptr of raylib.Color with as_void, count
        calling raylib.UnloadImagePalette with raw
        return owned

