    calling raylib.UnloadImage with image

## Loads an image from a file.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `path`: the file to load
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with a valid image, or `maybe none` when raylib fails.
##
## ## Notes
## The supported formats are the ones raylib was built with, normally PNG, BMP, TGA, GIF, QOI, JPG and PSF.
## `maybe none` when the file is missing or the format is unsupported.
##
## ## Memory
## Nothing is leaked: every raylib buffer this wrapper allocates or receives is released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var img as maybe raylib.Image is calling raylibx_images.load_image with "art.png"
## ```

weave load_image with path as string into maybe raylib.Image:
    let c_path as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with path
    var img as raylib.Image is calling raylib.LoadImage with c_path
    if calling raylib.IsImageValid with img:
        return some img
    return maybe none

