## Encodes an image into a byte buffer in memory.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `image`: the image to encode
## - `file_type`: the extension to encode as, for example `".png"`
##
## ## Returns
## `some` with an owned `list of byte`, or `maybe none` when raylib fails to encode.
##
## ## Notes
## raylib reports the buffer length through an out-parameter; the wrapper folds it into `.length` and copies the bytes into an owned list, releasing the raylib buffer.
## `maybe none` when raylib fails to encode.
##
## ## Memory
## Nothing is leaked: every raylib buffer this wrapper allocates or receives is released before returning.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var blob as maybe (list of byte) is calling raylibx_images.export_image_to_memory with img, ".png"
## ```

weave export_image_to_memory with image as raylib.Image, file_type as string into maybe (list of byte):
    let c_file_type as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with file_type
    var n as int is 0
    var raw as ref to byte is calling raylib.ExportImageToMemory with image, c_file_type, sigil of n
    if calling ffi.is_null with (transmute raw to ref to void):
        return maybe none
    let as_void as ref to void is transmute raw to ref to void
    var owned as list of byte is calling ffi.list_of_bytes_from_ptr with as_void, n
    calling raylib.MemFree with as_void
    return some owned

